    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Outpaint by pixels (whole picture, in-budget)\n\nThe four **`outpaint_*_px` INT nodes** are the only knobs: pixels to add per side. Math nodes convert them to the crop node's factors (`f = 1 + N/W`) and everything downstream (canvas size, target) follows automatically - change one N, one graph moves. Sampling is **native** (`output_resize_to_target_size` off): the model paints the canvas at its true size.\n\n- **Budget is your responsibility:** keep `(W + N_left + N_right) x (H + N_up + N_down) <= ~1.5 MP` (SDXL degrades beyond that). On a 1024x1024 source, ~+160 px per side is safe; keep canvas sides multiples of 64.\n- With all N = 0 the flow does nothing (factors 1.0) - a coherent empty default.\n- For **large sources / extending only part of the picture**, use `outpaint-fragment.json` instead.\n- The original region comes back untouched (stitcher); the new area is invented.\n\n*How to run it: story **S5** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E41** in `2d/EXPERIMENTS-2D.md`.*"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## Outpaint by pixels (whole picture, in-budget)\n\nThe four **`outpaint_*_px` INT nodes** are the only knobs: pixels to add per side. Math nodes convert them to the crop node's factors (`f = 1 + N/W`) and everything downstream (canvas size, target) follows automatically - change one N, one graph moves. Sampling is **native** (`output_resize_to_target_size` off): the model paints the canvas at its true size.\n\n- **Budget is your responsibility:** keep `(W + N_left + N_right) x (H + N_up + N_down) <= ~1.5 MP` (SDXL degrades beyond that). On a 1024x1024 source, ~+160 px per side is safe; keep canvas sides multiples of 64.\n- With all N = 0 the flow does nothing (factors 1.0) - a coherent empty default.\n- For **large sources / extending only part of the picture**, use `outpaint-fragment.json` instead.\n- The original region comes back untouched (stitcher); the new area is invented.\n\n*How to run it: story **S5** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E41** in `2d/EXPERIMENTS-2D.md`.*"
   },
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  }
